jobs.instructions:
Applications should be submitted as a single PDF containing the following documents:

- Cover letter;
- CV;
- A short research proposal describing the research that the candidate plans to carry out in the next 4 years (2000 words max.);
- A sample of written work (8000 words max). This may be a part of a PhD thesis.

Application review will begin on October 7, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Candidates should submit a: 

Letter of application that (a) describes their teaching interests, experience, and philosophy, especially in relation to teaching ethics; (b) summarizes their current and future scholarship; and (c) explains their approach to contributing to their academic communities; 

CV;
 
List of three references. 

All materials should be uploaded through Interfolio at https://apply.interfolio.com/192084. For more information, please contact Prof. Howard Pickett ([email protected]). Semi-finalists will be asked to supply three confidential letters of recommendation and a writing sample before their interview.
